{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מזקן", :translit "m'ziknei", :gloss "from old age"} {:he "חסר", :translit "chaser", :gloss "defective / missing-letter"} {:he "ויהי כי זקן יצחק ותכהין עיניו מראות", :translit "vayehi ki zakhein yitzchak vatikh'eina einav meir'ot", :gloss "and it came to pass that when Isaac was old and his eyes were dim from seeing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word written defective (מזקן without the yod), evoking the episode of Isaac's dimmed eyes (Genesis 27:1)."}], :frame {:text "The spelling מזקן (defective, without yod) links Jacob's old-age blindness to Isaac's blindness at Genesis 27:1, where Jacob disguised himself to obtain the blessing (Genesis 27:1–29). Joseph likewise reversed expectation when blessing Jacob's grandsons, placing the younger Ephraim ahead of the elder Manasseh (Genesis 48:13–20).", :sources ["Genesis 27:1" "Genesis 48:13–20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word written defective (מזקן without the yod), evoking the episode of Isaac's dimmed eyes (Genesis 27:1).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:03.062995742Z", :model "glm-5.2"}